    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d356">

                <pb facs="0415" n="331" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg331"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.54262/169</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Willard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1159</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-04-18">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 18, 1918</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received May 18.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Embassy’s despatch No.
                    1060, of January 15, 1918,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d356-f1"/> and the Department’s
                    telegram No. 950, of March 11, 1918,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d356-f2"/> concerning
                    “Trading with the Enemy Act,” which was transmitted to the German Government
                    through the Spanish Embassy in Berlin, I have the honor to enclose herewith a
                    copy of the reply received from the German Foreign Office to which a copy of the
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Reichs-Gesetzblatt</hi> No. 2, is attached.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph E. Willard</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d356-a1.xml" xpointer="d356-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
